From e4c9b62669526f229b8f63b4da57a9c801dd493f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: rkvenc forward-port <forward-port@local>
Date: Tue, 21 Jul 2026 17:27:13 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] video: rockchip: mpp: guard the wait-result path against a
 device-less session

mpp_wait_result_default() fetches the task's device with
mpp_get_task_used_device() and then dereferences it unconditionally
(if (mpp->dev_ops->result)), exactly like the async worker did before
the preceding fix. It is the synchronous twin of that bug: a pending
task whose session has no bound device NULL-derefs here on the
poll/wait path instead of in the worker kthread.

Guard it right after the device is fetched -- before the poll and the
blocking wait -- so a device-less task is failed and dropped in every
mode rather than dereferencing NULL or lingering unpollable in the
pending list. mpp_free_task() already tolerates a NULL device (from the
worker fix), so popping the dead task here is safe.

This was not the observed crash (that path is synchronous and would have
faulted in the decode ioctl, whereas the reported fault was the ~47 s
deferred worker), but it is the same bug class on the sibling path and
must not be left as a second way to oops on a torn-down session.

Signed-off-by: rkvenc forward-port <forward-port@local>
---
 drivers/video/rockchip/mpp/mpp_common.c | 13 +++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 13 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/video/rockchip/mpp/mpp_common.c b/drivers/video/rockchip/mpp/mpp_common.c
index f19728d8f73e1..b981bcbb1ae94 100644
--- a/drivers/video/rockchip/mpp/mpp_common.c
+++ b/drivers/video/rockchip/mpp/mpp_common.c
@@ -1080,6 +1080,19 @@ static int mpp_wait_result_default(struct mpp_session *session,
 		return -EIO;
 	}
 	mpp = mpp_get_task_used_device(task, session);
+	if (unlikely(!mpp)) {
+		/*
+		 * The task's session has no bound device, so it can never be
+		 * completed; fail it here instead of dereferencing a NULL
+		 * device in the result path below. This is the synchronous
+		 * twin of the worker NULL-deref guarded alongside this change;
+		 * drop the dead task so it does not linger in the pending list.
+		 */
+		mpp_err("session %d:%d task has no device\n",
+			session->device_type, session->index);
+		mpp_session_pop_pending(session, task);
+		return -EIO;
+	}
 
 	if (msgs->flags & MPP_FLAGS_POLL_NON_BLOCK) {
 		if (!test_bit(TASK_STATE_DONE, &task->state))
-- 
